    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s requirements meticulously. The core directive is about card manipulation \342\200\223 shrinking and expanding, with specific visual behaviors in the \"InProgress\" state. The challenge lies in translating these specifications into concrete design elements, especially the progress bar visualization for shrunk cards. I\'m focusing on the user\'s explicit instructions.\n\n\n**Refining Display Logic**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the visual aspect of the shrunk cards. The objective is to ensure the card\'s name remains visible in the shrunk state. In the \"Completed\" column, shrunk cards will be entirely green with white text. I\'m exploring an efficient implementation to toggle between expanded and shrunk views, considering both global and individual card controls, using a flexible board-level view mode and individual overrides.\n\n\n**Visualizing Compact Cards**\n\nI\'m now determining what information to display in each card state. When expanded, I\'ll keep the full card details. When shrunk, I\'ll only show the card\'s title prominently, but still allow for a subtle drag handle and quick action buttons on hover or the right side. The InProgress shrunk card will function as a progress bar, with the background filling to represent completion. The card\'s name must remain visible.\n\n\n"
